{"id":"mahabharata-3-206","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":206,"title":"षडधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 206 · Kaushika returns home","summary":{"en":"The hunter tells how the sage, appeased, promised he would remember his past and be freed after this birth. Kaushika honours him as a true Brahmin by conduct and returns home to serve his parents; Yudhishthira declares he never tires of such stories.","kn":"ಶಾಂತಗೊಂಡ ಋಷಿ ತನಗೆ ಪೂರ್ವಜನ್ಮಸ್ಮರಣೆ ಇರುವುದು, ಈ ಜನ್ಮದ ನಂತರ ಮುಕ್ತಿ ಎಂದು ವಾಗ್ದಾನ ಮಾಡಿದ್ದನ್ನು ವ್ಯಾಧನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ನಡತೆಯಿಂದ ನಿಜ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನೆಂದು ಅವನನ್ನು ಗೌರವಿಸಿ ಕೌಶಿಕನು ತಂದೆತಾಯಿಯರ ಸೇವೆಗೆ ಮನೆಗೆ ಮರಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಇಂಥ ಕಥೆಗಳಿಂದ ತನಗೆಂದೂ ತೃಪ್ತಿಯಿಲ್ಲ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ.","hi":"व्याध बताता है कि प्रसन्न हुए ऋषि ने वचन दिया था कि उसे पूर्वजन्म स्मरण रहेगा और इस जन्म के बाद वह मुक्त होगा। कौशिक उसे आचरण से सच्चा ब्राह्मण मानकर सम्मान देते हैं और माता-पिता की सेवा के लिए घर लौटते हैं; युधिष्ठिर कहते हैं कि ऐसी कथाओं से उनका मन कभी नहीं भरता।","te":"శాంతించిన ఋషి తనకు పూర్వజన్మస్మృతి ఉంటుందని, ఈ జన్మ తర్వాత విముక్తి కలుగుతుందని వాగ్దానం చేసినట్లు వ్యాధుడు చెబుతాడు. ప్రవర్తనతో నిజమైన బ్రాహ్మణుడని అతనిని గౌరవించి కౌశికుడు తల్లిదండ్రుల సేవకై ఇంటికి తిరిగివెళ్తాడు; ఇలాంటి కథలతో తనకు ఎన్నడూ తృప్తి కలగదని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అంటాడు.","ta":"சாந்தமடைந்த முனிவர் தனக்கு முற்பிறவி நினைவு இருக்கும் என்றும் இப்பிறவிக்குப் பின் விடுதலை கிடைக்கும் என்றும் வாக்களித்ததாக வ்யாதன் சொல்கிறான். ஒழுக்கத்தால் உண்மையான அந்தணன் என்று அவனைக் கௌரவித்துக் கௌஶிகர் பெற்றோருக்குப் பணிவிடை செய்ய வீடு திரும்புகிறார்; இத்தகைய கதைகளால் தமக்கு ஒருபோதும் சலிப்பில்லை என்கிறார் யுதிஷ்டிரர்.","ml":"മുനി ശാന്തനായി, ഈ ജന്മത്തിനുശേഷം പൂർവജന്മം ഓർക്കുമെന്നും മോചിതനാകുമെന്നും വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്തതായി വ്യാധൻ പറയുന്നു. നടപടിയിലൂടെ യഥാർത്ഥ ബ്രാഹ്മണനായി കൗശികൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ ബഹുമാനിക്കുന്നു, മാതാപിതാക്കളെ സേവിക്കാൻ വീട്ടിലേക്ക് മടങ്ങുന്നു; ഇത്തരം കഥകൾ കേട്ട് തനിക്ക് മടുപ്പില്ലെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.206; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"व्याध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवं शप्तोऽहमृषिणा तदा द्विजवरोत्तम ।\nअभिप्रसादयमृषिं गिरा वाक्यविशारदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So the sage cursed me then, best of brahmins, and I tried to win him over with words, for he was skilled in speech.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"अजानता मयाकार्यमिदमद्य कृतं मुने ।\nक्षन्तुमर्हसि तत्सर्वं प्रसीद भगवन्निति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I said: 'Sage, I did this wrong today without knowing it. Please forgive all of it; be gracious, blessed one.'\""}},{"text":"ऋषिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"The sage said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"नान्यथा भविता शाप एवमेतदसंशयम् ।\nआनृशंस्यादहं किंचित्कर्तानुग्रहमद्य ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The curse cannot be otherwise; it will be so, without doubt. But out of compassion I will show you some favor today.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"शूद्रयोनौ वर्तमानो धर्मज्ञो भविता ह्यसि ।\nमातापित्रोश्च शुश्रूषां करिष्यसि न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Living in a shudra birth you will still know dharma, and you will certainly serve your mother and father.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"तया शुश्रूषया सिद्धिं महतीं समवाप्स्यसि ।\nजातिस्मरश्च भविता स्वर्गं चैव गमिष्यसि ।\nशापक्षयान्ते निर्वृत्ते भवितासि पुनर्द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By that service you will gain great perfection. You will remember your past births and go to heaven. When the curse is spent and finished, you will become a brahmin again.\""}},{"text":"व्याध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"एवं शप्तः पुरा तेन ऋषिणास्म्युग्रतेजसा ।\nप्रसादश्च कृतस्तेन ममैवं द्विपदां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That is how the fiercely radiant sage cursed me long ago, and how he showed me grace too, best of men.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"शरं चोद्धृतवानस्मि तस्य वै द्विजसत्तम ।\nआश्रमं च मया नीतो न च प्राणैर्व्ययुज्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I pulled the arrow out of him, best of brahmins, and brought him to his hermitage; he did not lose his life.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"एतत्ते सर्वमाख्यातं यथा मम पुराभवत् ।\nअभितश्चापि गन्तव्यं मया स्वर्गं द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I have told you all that happened to me before. In any case I am bound for heaven, best of brahmins.\""}},{"text":"ब्राह्मण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"एवमेतानि पुरुषा दुःखानि च सुखानि च ।\nप्राप्नुवन्ति महाबुद्धे नोत्कण्ठां कर्तुमर्हसि ।\nदुष्करं हि कृतं तात जानता जातिमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Men meet sorrows and joys like these, wise one; you should not be restless. It was hard to carry this out while knowing your own birth.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"कर्मदोषश्च वै विद्वन्नात्मजातिकृतेन वै ।\nकंचित्कालं मृष्यतां वै ततोऽसि भविता द्विजः ।\nसांप्रतं च मतो मेऽसि ब्राह्मणो नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The fault lies in deeds, learned one, not in the birth you were given. Bear it for a while; then you will be a brahmin again. As of now I consider you a brahmin, with no doubt.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"ब्राह्मणः पतनीयेषु वर्तमानो विकर्मसु ।\nदाम्भिको दुष्कृतप्रायः शूद्रेण सदृशो भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A brahmin who engages in degrading acts, who is hypocritical and mostly does evil, becomes like a shudra.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"यस्तु शूद्रो दमे सत्ये धर्मे च सततोत्थितः ।\nतं ब्राह्मणमहं मन्ये वृत्तेन हि भवेद्द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But a shudra who is always steady in self-control, truth and dharma I consider a brahmin, for one becomes twice-born by conduct.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"कर्मदोषेण विषमां गतिमाप्नोति दारुणाम् ।\nक्षीणदोषमहं मन्ये चाभितस्त्वां नरोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By the fault of deeds one reaches a harsh, uneven fate. I think your fault is exhausted, best of men.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"कर्तुमर्हसि नोत्कण्ठां त्वद्विधा ह्यविषादिनः ।\nलोकवृत्तान्तवृत्तज्ञा नित्यं धर्मपरायणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You should not fret; men like you are never despondent, know how the world goes, and are always devoted to dharma.\""}},{"text":"व्याध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"प्रज्ञया मानसं दुःखं हन्याच्छारीरमौषधैः ।\nएतद्विज्ञानसामर्थ्यं न बालैः समतां व्रजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"One should destroy mental pain with wisdom and bodily pain with medicine. This is the power of knowledge; children cannot match it.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"अनिष्टसंप्रयोगाच्च विप्रयोगात्प्रियस्य च ।\nमानुषा मानसैर्दुःखैर्युज्यन्ते अल्पबुद्धयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Through meeting what they dislike and parting from what they love, men of small understanding are joined to mental sorrows.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"गुणैर्भूतानि युज्यन्ते वियुज्यन्ते तथैव च ।\nसर्वाणि नैतदेकस्य शोकस्थानं हि विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Beings are joined to qualities and parted from them in the same way; this is true of all, so grief has no place for any single person.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"अनिष्टेनान्वितं पश्यंस्तथा क्षिप्रं विरज्यते ।\nततश्च प्रतिकुर्वन्ति यदि पश्यन्त्युपक्रमम् ।\nशोचतो न भवेत्किंचित्केवलं परितप्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"One who sees himself bound up with something unwelcome soon turns away from it. People then remedy it if they see a way. Grieving achieves nothing; it only torments.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"परित्यजन्ति ये दुःखं सुखं वाप्युभयं नराः ।\nत एव सुखमेधन्ते ज्ञानतृप्ता मनीषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Those who give up both pain and pleasure grow happy; they are wise and content with knowledge.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"असंतोषपरा मूढाः संतोषं यान्ति पण्डिताः ।\nअसंतोषस्य नास्त्यन्तस्तुष्टिस्तु परमं सुखम् ।\nन शोचन्ति गताध्वानः पश्यन्तः परमां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Fools are bent on discontent; the learned reach contentment. Discontent has no end, while satisfaction is the highest happiness. Those who have traveled the road, seeing the highest goal, do not grieve.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"न विषादे मनः कार्यं विषादो विषमुत्तमम् ।\nमारयत्यकृतप्रज्ञं बालं क्रुद्ध इवोरगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Do not give the mind to despair. Despair is a supreme poison; it kills the unwise, as an angry snake kills a child.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"यं विषादोऽभिभवति विषमे समुपस्थिते ।\nतेजसा तस्य हीनस्य पुरुषार्थो न विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The man whom despair overpowers when trouble comes is drained of vigor and has no human effort left.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"अवश्यं क्रियमाणस्य कर्मणो दृश्यते फलम् ।\nन हि निर्वेदमागम्य किंचित्प्राप्नोति शोभनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The fruit of an act that must be done is seen; no one who gives way to dejection gains anything good.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"अथाप्युपायं पश्येत दुःखस्य परिमोक्षणे ।\nअशोचन्नारभेतैव युक्तश्चाव्यसनी भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Even so, if one sees a means of freeing oneself from sorrow, one should begin it without grieving, staying focused and free from distress.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"भूतेष्वभावं संचिन्त्य ये तु बुद्धेः परं गताः ।\nन शोचन्ति कृतप्रज्ञाः पश्यन्तः परमां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Those who have gone beyond intellect, reflecting that beings come from non-being, do not grieve; they are accomplished in wisdom and see the highest goal.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"न शोचामि च वै विद्वन्कालाकाङ्क्षी स्थितोऽस्म्यहम् ।\nएतैर्निदर्शनैर्ब्रह्मन्नावसीदामि सत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I do not grieve, learned one; I wait for my time. By such reasoning, brahmin, I do not sink into despair, best of men.\""}},{"text":"ब्राह्मण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"कृतप्रज्ञोऽसि मेधावी बुद्धिश्च विपुला तव ।\nनाहं भवन्तं शोचामि ज्ञानतृप्तोऽसि धर्मवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You are accomplished in wisdom, intelligent, and your understanding is vast. I do not grieve for you; you are satisfied with knowledge and know dharma.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"आपृच्छे त्वां स्वस्ति तेऽस्तु धर्मस्त्वा परिरक्षतु ।\nअप्रमादस्तु कर्तव्यो धर्मे धर्मभृतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I take my leave of you; may you fare well, and may dharma protect you. Be vigilant in dharma, best of those who uphold it.\""}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":29,"text":"बाढमित्येव तं व्याधः कृताञ्जलिरुवाच ह ।\nप्रदक्षिणमथो कृत्वा प्रस्थितो द्विजसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'So be it,' said the hunter with joined palms. The best of brahmins circled him to the right and departed.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"स तु गत्वा द्विजः सर्वां शुश्रूषां कृतवांस्तदा ।\nमातापितृभ्यां वृद्धाभ्यां यथान्यायं सुसंशितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The brahmin went home and, with a keen and steady mind, served his aged mother and father fully and properly.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"एतत्ते सर्वमाख्यातं निखिलेन युधिष्ठिर ।\nपृष्टवानसि यं तात धर्मं धर्मभृतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I have told you all of it, Yudhishthira, the dharma you asked about, best of those who uphold dharma.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"पतिव्रताया माहात्म्यं ब्राह्मणस्य च सत्तम ।\nमातापित्रोश्च शुश्रूषा व्याधे धर्मश्च कीर्तितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The greatness of the devoted wife and of the brahmin, and the service of mother and father, and the dharma of the hunter have all been described, good man.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":33,"text":"अत्यद्भुतमिदं ब्रह्मन्धर्माख्यानमनुत्तमम् ।\nसर्वधर्मभृतां श्रेष्ठ कथितं द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brahmin, this teaching of dharma is most wonderful and unsurpassed; you have told it, best of upholders of all dharmas.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"सुखश्रव्यतया विद्वन्मुहूर्तमिव मे गतम् ।\nन हि तृप्तोऽस्मि भगवञ्शृण्वानो धर्ममुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"It was so pleasant to hear, learned sir, that it seemed to last only a moment. Venerable one, I am not satisfied with hearing the highest dharma.\""}}]}]}